        "contenuto_esteso": "New York City Zohran Mamdani (D) said Wednesday he would ask King Charles III to return the Koh-i-noor diamond if given the opportunity. The diamond, which weighs 105.6 carats, has been in the possession of the British government since the mid-1800s, according to Smithsonian Magazine. The gem originally came from the alluvial mines in India..."
